{#-
  Shared inline-SVG icon set — monoline, 24×24, stroke=currentColor so every icon
  inherits its context's text colour (theme light/dark + zh 红涨绿跌 flips come free).
  Import the macro:  {% from "_icons.html.j2" import icon %}   then  {{ icon('search') }}
  Base CSS (.ic-svg / sizing / .ic-spin) lives on the consuming page for now — this is
  the Canada icon-system testing ground (2026-07-24); promote to theme.css when rolled
  out site-wide. `cls` appends utility classes (e.g. colour: ic-up / ic-dn / ic-mut).
  target/star/diamond/swirl/map/bars/list (2026-08-03) are the monoline replacements for the
  emoji that were doing section-head duty on the Subsector Confluence desk — same idiom, so
  they inherit ink + theme + the zh 红涨绿跌 flip from currentColor like the rest. Their path
  data is mirrored byte-for-byte in templates/subsectors.js (`ICON_PATHS`), which draws the
  same glyphs client-side; keep the two in step.
  `sector` (2026-08-06) is the US Act-Now board's sector-fund mark, the monoline replacement
  for the classical-building emoji that row/shelf/hover-card marks used before the doctrine
  §5.8 sweep. It is drawn SERVER-SIDE only, so it is deliberately NOT mirrored
  into subsectors.js — that mirror exists for the glyphs subsectors.js draws itself, and
  copying a glyph nothing reads there would rot. Legibility budget: it renders at 13px in
  row marks, so it stays at three columns with ~3-unit clear gaps at the 24-grid; a fourth
  column fuses into a grey slab at that size (measured, mockups/act-now-icon-sweep/).
-#}
